# Vitest writes snapshot files with LF. core.autocrlf=true checks them out
# with CRLF. The two disagree on every run: the content hash still matches
# HEAD so nothing is ever staged, but git status shows the file modified
# indefinitely and update-index --refresh reports "needs update".
#
# That is a false positive on the file whose whole job is to be the zero-diff
# gate, and one that looks exactly like the regression it exists to catch.
# Pinning the worktree form to LF -- the form the tool already writes --
# removes the disagreement. The committed blob is already all-LF, so no
# renormalising commit is needed. See audit 2.4.136.
*.snap text eol=lf
